      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 IMSS. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "BACKGROUND AND AIMS",
            "content": "The SNP rs662 in the paraoxonase 1 gene (PON1 Q192R) has been associated with obesity, dyslipidemia and cardiovascular risk. In this study, DNA samples of 117 children aged 6 to 12 years from San Luis Potosí, México were genotyped for Q192R polymorphism of the PON1 gene."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "Genotypic frequencies were determined by allelic discrimination assay by real-time PCR using TaqMan fluorogenic probes. Anthropometry, lipid profile, glucose and insulin were analyzed by genotype."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "The distribution of allele frequency in the population was Q = 65 and R = 35 following the Hardy Weinberg equilibrium (χ(2) = 3.15, p = 0.076). The Homeostasis Model Assessment for Insulin Resistance (HOMA-IR) index showed statistically significant differences among QQ/QR/RR genotypes (p = 0.032). The odds ratio for the carriers of the RR genotype was associated with HOMA-IR corresponding to the 95(th) percentile or higher for Mexican children based on sex and age (OR = 4.68; 95% confidence intervals, 1.23-17.8; p = 0.016). When the absolute mean of HOMAR-IR was set as the cutoff, an increased odds was observed (OR = 6.52; 95% confidence intervals, 1.68-25.3; p = 0.008)."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "content": "According to our results, PON1 Q192R polymorphism is a risk marker for insulin resistance, a pathological factor involved in the development of metabolic syndrome."
          }
        ]
      },
